Offsets: the intersection of the offsets of a convex crease's faces that
become tangent past the solid's end keeps only the branch along the crease
(mitcad#1184).

The case: a loft from an octagon to a circle (BRepOffsetAPI_ThruSections),
shelled 3 mm inwards with both its ends removed, or offset inwards closed.
At the octagon's corners the loft's ruled faces meet at convex creases that
flatten to tangency at the circle. Where the walls lean out towards the
circle, the inward offsets of the two faces at a corner become tangent a
little past the circle's end (0.16 mm past it for the 3 mm wall) and cross
there. BRepOffset_Inter3d::ConnexIntByInt intersects the enlarged offset
faces: the branch along the corner and five to seven more pieces about and
past the tangency, up to the enlarged faces' ends, all connected, so that
CheckIntersFF keeps them all. From them MakeLoops rebuilt no inner face for
most walls: the thick solid was not done (BRepOffset_UnknownError) or came
out invalid (the body with offset faces of no area), a Geom_OffsetSurface
evaluation failed on a vertex of such a piece (UpdateTolerance), and the
closed offset was null or invalid, at every thickness from 0.5 mm. A
square to a circle that it surrounds failed the same way.

BRepOffset_Tool::Inter3D now keeps only the branch along the edge there
(the new DropCrossingsPastTangentEnd, after CheckIntersFF): of the edges
nearest to the edge's middle (a curve the pave filler gives twice, once run
on past the tangency, the one that runs least far past the end) and the
edges it goes on into towards the edge's other end where no other edge
meets them. It acts only where the edge's two faces have parallel normals
(within 1e-4) at one end of it and not at its middle, the intersection gave
more than one edge, and that branch runs past the plane of the solid's end
there, the osculating plane of the face's boundary at that end. Where the
offsets become tangent before the end (walls leaning in, the end's own
offset cutting the branch first), and for every other edge, the
intersection is as before. The shells are valid, both ends open, the inner
walls the thickness from the outer ones within 1e-6 mm.
